# Agent code style

Apply `agent-code-style.md` to every implementation and code review.

- Name every private field with a leading underscore in camelCase: `_poolManager`.
- Name every constant in `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`: `TARGET_DISTANCE`.
- Use `PascalCase` for public types, methods, and properties.
- Name every event in `PascalCase` with an `On` prefix: `OnCurrentWaveChanged`.
- Use `camelCase` for parameters and local variables.
- Name `CancellationToken` values `ct` and `CancellationTokenSource` values `cts`; use `_cts` for a private source field.
- Name interfaces with an `I` prefix.
- Put every public class in its own matching C# file. Private nested types are allowed.
- Never add generic `Scripts`, `Code`, or `Source` folders. Place code in the folder of its feature or mechanic.
- Organize `Assets` by game feature or mechanic, never by resource type.
- Do not add top-level `Scripts`, `Prefabs`, or `Textures` folders.
- Keep scripts with the prefab and resources of their feature. Put shared features higher in the hierarchy and object-specific resources in nested object folders.
- Do not introduce static state for gameplay systems.
